Many thanks to the development team for 3.0h, patchlevel 6.  The graphics
option is now fixed and it was broken since patch 4 for many of us.

The new door code allows diagonal access if there is *no* door.  If
there is an open door, then entry must be straight on.  The default
characters for no door, open vertical door, and open horizontal door
are spaces which is the same as solid rock.  If you wander down a
corridor, the open/no door will appear as solid rock with the default
graphic characters.  If you use the / command to identify the location
of said open/no door, you will get the same response as identifying
solid rock or an unexplored area of the dungeon (that is, it just ends
the identify mode).   While this is argueably a bug, everything works
fine if the three symbols for open/no doors are properly defined according
to your tastes.

The following file elucidates the graphics characters, their default
setting, and a possible setting for vt100 and wyse50 style terminals.
The characters for up and down ladders are .ge. and .le. signs,
respectively.  I chose no door to be like a corridor and open doors
to be the diamond symbol (vt100) and a dot (wyse50).  The Guidebook
covers this information, but spaces are collapsed on printout.  In addition,
I hope the following tabular form will assist nethackers.
#---cut here, of course---
#!/bin/sh
# shar:	Shell Archiver  (v1.22)
#
#	Run the following text with /bin/sh to create:
#	  graphics
#
sed 's/^X//' << 'SHAR_EOF' > graphics &&
X                  Nethack 3.0h Patchlevel 6 Graphics Characters
X==============================================================================
XObject                Default    vt100     Wyse50
X______________________________________________________________________________
Xsolid rock              " "      " "       " "
Xvertical wall            |       \mx       \m6
Xhorizontal wall          -       \mq       \m:
Xupper left corner        -       \ml       \m2
Xupper right corner       -       \mk       \m3
Xlower left corner        -       \mm       \m1
Xlower right corner       -       \mj       \m5
Xcross wall               -       \mn       \m8
Xupward T wall            -       \mv       \m0
Xdownward T wall          -       \mw       \m=
Xleftward T wall          -       \mu       \m4
Xrightward T wall         -       \mt       \m9
Xvertical beam            |       \mx       \m6
Xhorizontal beam          -       \mq       \m:
Xleft slant               \\       \\        \\
Xright slant              /        /         /
Xno door                 " "      \ma       \m?
Xvertical open door      " "      \m`        .
Xhorizontal open door    " "      \m`        .
Xclosed door              +        +         +
Xfloor of a room          .       \m~        .
Xcorridor                 #       \ma       \m;
Xstairs up                <        <
Xstairs down              >        >
Xtrap                     ^        ^
Xweb                      "        "
Xpool or moat             }        }
Xfountain                 {        {
Xkitchen sink             #        #
Xthrone                   \\       \\
Xaltar                    _        _
Xladder up                <       \my
Xladder down              >       \mz
Xvertical drawbridge      #
Xhorizontal drawbridge    #
X______________________________________________________________________________
X" " means type a space in your NETHACKOPTIONS graphics variable
XOther characters are typed as shown.
SHAR_EOF
chmod 0644 graphics || echo "restore of graphics fails"
set `wc -c graphics`;Sum=$1
if test "$Sum" != "1934"
then echo original size 1934, current size $Sum;fi
exit 0
